{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `e2ba27f8`: accepted as the documented limit of CB-2.\n\n1. The card. When the card changed between the member's view and\n   the press, the card sends no message and asks the member to\n   press again. The member then hands off what the member sees.\n2. The host. A message that names an earlier revision keeps that\n   revision as its subject. The host does not read it as the latest\n   revision, and it is no authorization. Before a typed submission\n   the host reads the current card and states the difference.\n3. The signature stays guarded where it is today: the typed\n   submission refuses a stale revision before it signs. Items 1\n   and 2 add words for the member and change no guard.\n4. Where it is written: the page that a host author reads for card\n   messages, in one short section. The repository's chat host stays\n   as it is in CB-2. If you find that it must compare the revision\n   to keep item 2 true in a test, tell me first.\n\nThe plan of the browser witness is accepted: the press of Report\nacross the existing refresh points, the native click observed, and\na control that restores the whole-root replacement.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}